      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Account is a special account for the purposes of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013.\nNote:\nAn Appropriation Act may contain a provision to the effect that, if any\nof the purposes of a special account is a purpose that is covered by an\nitem in the Appropriation Act (whether or not the item expressly refers\nto the special account), then amounts may be debited against the\nappropriation for that item and credited to that special account."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-11-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-11-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-11-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "imposes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Duty to debit and credit",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Investments of the Fund",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019#sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, invest\namounts standing to the credit of the Account in any authorised\ndebt security.\n\n(2) Investments under subsection (1) are taken to be investments of the\nFund.\n\n(3) At any time before an investment of the Fund matures, the Minister\nmay, on behalf of the Commonwealth, authorise the re-investment\nof the proceeds upon maturity in an authorised debt security with\nthe same entity. The new investment is taken to be an investment\nof the Fund.\n\n(4) An authorised debt security is a debt security that:\n\n(a) is issued by:\n\n(i) a trustee of a trust; or\n\n(ii) a body corporate that is a special purpose vehicle; and\n\n(b) is expressed in Australian dollars; and\n\n(c) relates to one or more amounts of credit provided (whether\nsecured or unsecured) to one or more debtors where each\nsuch amount of credit:\n\n(i) is provided wholly or predominantly for business\npurposes; and\n\n\nThe Australian Business Securitisation Fund  Part 2\n\nSection 13\n\nNo. 46, 2019\nAustralian Business Securitisation Fund Act 2019\n\n(ii) is less than $5 million or, if the rules prescribe another\namount of money, is less than that amount; and\n\n(iii) complies with any other requirements or restrictions\nprescribed by the rules; and\n\n(d) complies with any other requirements or restrictions\nprescribed by the rules.\n\n(5) Section 58 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with investment by the\nCommonwealth) does not apply to an investment of the Fund.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, invest\namounts standing to the credit of the Account in any authorised\ndebt security.\n\n(2) Investments under subsection (1) are taken to be investments of the\nFund.\n\n(3) At any time before an investment of the Fund matures, the Minister\nmay, on behalf of the Commonwealth, authorise the re-investment\nof the proceeds upon maturity in an authorised debt security with\nthe same entity. The new investment is taken to be an investment\nof the Fund.\n\n(4) An authorised debt security is a debt security that:\n\n(a) is issued by:\n\n(i) a trustee of a trust; or\n\n(ii) a body corporate that is a special purpose vehicle; and\n\n(b) is expressed in Australian dollars; and\n\n(c) relates to one or more amounts of credit provided (whether\nsecured or unsecured) to one or more debtors where each\nsuch amount of credit:\n\n(i) is provided wholly or predominantly for business\npurposes; and\n\n\nThe Australian Business Securitisation Fund  Part 2\n\nSection 13\n\nNo. 46, 2019\nAustralian Business Securitisation Fund Act 2019\n\n(ii) is less than $5 million or, if the rules prescribe another\namount of money, is less than that amount; and\n\n(iii) complies with any other requirements or restrictions\nprescribed by the rules; and\n\n(d) complies with any other requirements or restrictions\nprescribed by the rules.\n\n(5) Section 58 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with investment by the\nCommonwealth) does not apply to an investment of the Fund.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-12-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-12-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-12-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-12-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-12-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ae90db62f434083ad16ada026d457fe9fff79b43da777b5a2f0dae86184209b1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019#sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Investments of the Fund",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, on behalf of the Commonwealth, invest\namounts standing to the credit of the Account in any authorised\ndebt security.\n\n(2) Investments under subsection (1) are taken to be investments of the\nFund.\n\n(3) At any time before an investment of the Fund matures, the Minister\nmay, on behalf of the Commonwealth, authorise the re-investment\nof the proceeds upon maturity in an authorised debt security with\nthe same entity. The new investment is taken to be an investment\nof the Fund.\n\n(4) An authorised debt security is a debt security that:\n\n(a) is issued by:\n\n(i) a trustee of a trust; or\n\n(ii) a body corporate that is a special purpose vehicle; and\n\n(b) is expressed in Australian dollars; and\n\n(c) relates to one or more amounts of credit provided (whether\nsecured or unsecured) to one or more debtors where each\nsuch amount of credit:\n\n(i) is provided wholly or predominantly for business\npurposes; and\n\n\nThe Australian Business Securitisation Fund  Part 2\n\nSection 13\n\nNo. 46, 2019\nAustralian Business Securitisation Fund Act 2019\n\n(ii) is less than $5 million or, if the rules prescribe another\namount of money, is less than that amount; and\n\n(iii) complies with any other requirements or restrictions\nprescribed by the rules; and\n\n(d) complies with any other requirements or restrictions\nprescribed by the rules.\n\n(5) Section 58 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013 (which deals with investment by the\nCommonwealth) does not apply to an investment of the Fund."
    },
