    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-13",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13 Investment Mandate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019#sec-13"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, give directions about\nthe exercise of the Minister’s powers under section 12. The\ndirections together constitute the Investment Mandate.\nNote:\nSection 42 (disallowance) and Part 4 of Chapter 3 (sunsetting) of the\nLegislation Act 2003 do not apply to the directions (see regulations\nmade for the purposes of paragraphs 44(2)(b) and 54(2)(b) of that\nAct).\n\n(2) The Minister must comply with the Investment Mandate.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), the Investment Mandate may\ninclude directions about any of the following:\n\n(a) strategies and policies to be followed for making\ninvestments;\n\n(b) decision-making criteria for making investments;\n\n(c) limits on making investments;\n\n(d) risk and return relating to investments;\n\n(e) governance arrangements relating to investments;\n\n(f) any other matters that the Minister thinks appropriate.\n\n(4) The Minister must not give a direction under subsection (1):\n\n(a) that has the purpose, or is likely to have the effect, of directly\nor indirectly requiring the Minister to make, or not to make, a\nparticular investment; or\n\n(b) that is inconsistent with this Act (including the objects of this\nAct).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, give directions about\nthe exercise of the Minister’s powers under section 12. The\ndirections together constitute the Investment Mandate.\nNote:\nSection 42 (disallowance) and Part 4 of Chapter 3 (sunsetting) of the\nLegislation Act 2003 do not apply to the directions (see regulations\nmade for the purposes of paragraphs 44(2)(b) and 54(2)(b) of that\nAct).\n\n(2) The Minister must comply with the Investment Mandate.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), the Investment Mandate may\ninclude directions about any of the following:\n\n(a) strategies and policies to be followed for making\ninvestments;\n\n(b) decision-making criteria for making investments;\n\n(c) limits on making investments;\n\n(d) risk and return relating to investments;\n\n(e) governance arrangements relating to investments;\n\n(f) any other matters that the Minister thinks appropriate.\n\n(4) The Minister must not give a direction under subsection (1):\n\n(a) that has the purpose, or is likely to have the effect, of directly\nor indirectly requiring the Minister to make, or not to make, a\nparticular investment; or\n\n(b) that is inconsistent with this Act (including the objects of this\nAct).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-13-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-13-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-13-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019-sec-13-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "709c539fa77fb0550e4c6ce26270435b96b2850cc17d675f2077c7628abf91a1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-business-securitisation-fund-act-2019#sec-13",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13 Investment Mandate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, give directions about\nthe exercise of the Minister’s powers under section 12. The\ndirections together constitute the Investment Mandate.\nNote:\nSection 42 (disallowance) and Part 4 of Chapter 3 (sunsetting) of the\nLegislation Act 2003 do not apply to the directions (see regulations\nmade for the purposes of paragraphs 44(2)(b) and 54(2)(b) of that\nAct).\n\n(2) The Minister must comply with the Investment Mandate.\n\n(3) Without limiting subsection (1), the Investment Mandate may\ninclude directions about any of the following:\n\n(a) strategies and policies to be followed for making\ninvestments;\n\n(b) decision-making criteria for making investments;\n\n(c) limits on making investments;\n\n(d) risk and return relating to investments;\n\n(e) governance arrangements relating to investments;\n\n(f) any other matters that the Minister thinks appropriate.\n\n(4) The Minister must not give a direction under subsection (1):\n\n(a) that has the purpose, or is likely to have the effect, of directly\nor indirectly requiring the Minister to make, or not to make, a\nparticular investment; or\n\n(b) that is inconsistent with this Act (including the objects of this\nAct)."
    },
